url: "https://github.com/marceloroldao/resolutive-science"
abstract: >-
  Resolutive Science v0.3.0 is an adversarial falsification release for the
  frozen one-parameter RCMS cosmological screening surrogate. It adds Protocols
  09–16, including null and injection/recovery calibration, equal-complexity
  functional controls, dataset-family ablations, systematics and amplitude
  stability tests, complexity-penalized model comparison, and a preregistered
  held-out BOSS DR12 prediction. The release preserves unfavorable outcomes:
  the logarithmic form is not uniquely selected, fitted amplitudes are not
  universal, model-selection preference over Lambda-CDM is not established,
  and the preregistered positive BOSS DR12 prediction is not reproduced within
  the frozen primary domain. This release does not claim discovery of new
  physics or experimental validation of Resolutive Physics.
